=== file lock setup ===
=== using-file-lock holds and releases ===
PASS: prober blocks while lock is held
PASS: prober acquires after the combinator returns normally
=== using-file-lock releases on throw ===
PASS: combinator re-throws the body error
PASS: prober acquires after the combinator throws
=== using-file-lock shared mode ===
PASS: shared-mode combinator runs and releases
=== try-file-lock acquired branch ===
PASS: try-file-lock takes acquired branch when free
=== try-file-lock missed branch ===
PASS: try-file-lock misses while another descriptor holds the lock
=== using-file-lock waits out contention ===
PASS: contended cooperative acquire eventually succeeds
=== using-file-lock releases on cancellation ===
PASS: lock released after task cancellation
=== file-lock-error on bad descriptor ===
PASS: bad descriptor raises file-lock-error
PASS: file-lock-error carries the ebadf name
PASS: file-lock-error carries the raw errno integer
=== try-file-lock file-lock-error on bad descriptor ===
PASS: try-file-lock bad descriptor raises file-lock-error
PASS: try-file-lock leaves only the caller's stream after a failed acquire
=== using-file-lock file-lock-error under a scheduler ===
PASS: cooperative acquire recorded one outcome
PASS: cooperative-path bad descriptor raises file-lock-error
=== using-file-lock cancellation while waiting ===
PASS: waiter recorded one outcome
PASS: waiter was cancelled while waiting, not acquired
